# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Viva
VIVA = [
 ("What exactly is G19 and why Gemma 1.0 2B-it?", "Original Gemma family, instruction-tuned, small enough for a 15 GB Colab T4 (about 5 GB in bf16). Later Gemma generations are different models, so they are not used."),
 ("Is Gemma open source?", "Open weights under the custom Gemma Terms of Use, gated on Hugging Face; not an OSI open-source licence."),
 ("Give Gemma 2B's architecture numbers.", "18 layers, d_model 2048, FFN 32,768, 8 heads, 1 KV head (multi-query), head size 256, vocab 256,128, 8192 context [GP]."),
 ("What is multi-query attention and why use it?", "All query heads share one K/V head, shrinking the KV cache and memory bandwidth at a small quality cost. Gemma 2B uses it; 7B uses full multi-head."),
 ("What is GeGLU?", "A gated feed-forward: gelu(xW_gate) * (xW_up) then a down projection. Gemma uses the approximate GeLU."),
 ("What is RMSNorm?", "Normalises by the root mean square without mean subtraction; Gemma code multiplies by (1 + scale)."),
 ("What is RoPE?", "Rotary position embedding: rotates query/key pairs by position-dependent angles so attention depends on relative offsets."),
 ("Why are embeddings tied and why scaled by sqrt(d)?", "Tying saves parameters (the 256k x 2048 matrix is ~524M); scaling by sqrt(embed_dim) in Embedder.encode keeps embedding magnitude compatible with the rest of the network."),
 ("Check Gemma's embedding parameter count.", "256,128 x 2,048 = 524,550,144, matching the paper's Table 2."),
 ("What are Gemma's chat control tokens?", "<start_of_turn> and <end_of_turn> with roles user and model; there is no system role in the card's format."),
 ("How was Gemma-it aligned?", "SFT on synthetic + human prompt-response pairs, then RLHF with a Bradley-Terry reward model [GP]."),
 ("What did the Gemma paper report for 2B on MMLU/GSM8K?", "MMLU 42.3 and GSM8K 17.7 for the pretrained 2B [GP Table 6] - literature, not our measurement."),
 ("What does G20's checkpoint name tell you?", "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B: distilled from R1, Qwen-architecture student, 7B; the base is Qwen2.5-Math-7B."),
 ("Was the 7B distilled model trained with RL?", "No. It got SFT only on ~800k R1-generated samples [DP 2.4]. RL (GRPO) was used for R1/R1-Zero."),
 ("Explain GRPO.", "Sample G outputs per question, score them, use A_i = (r_i - mean)/std as the advantage (no critic), PPO-style clipped ratio objective plus KL to a reference policy."),
 ("Why no critic model in GRPO?", "The group mean reward is the baseline, cutting memory/compute versus PPO's value network."),
 ("What is R1-Zero?", "RL applied directly to V3-Base with no SFT; it developed long reasoning and self-verification but had poor readability and language mixing."),
 ("Describe the four stages of R1.", "Cold-start SFT, reasoning RL, rejection-sampling SFT (~800k samples), all-scenario RL."),
 ("What rewards did R1-Zero use?", "Rule-based accuracy reward and a format reward for <think> tags; a language-consistency reward was added for R1."),
 ("Why not neural reward models early on?", "The paper cites reward hacking and the retraining cost; rule-based rewards are harder to game for verifiable tasks."),
 ("What is distillation here?", "Fine-tuning a small dense model on outputs of a stronger model; the paper found it beat running RL on the 32B base."),
 ("Which prompt rules does the README give?", "No system prompt, temperature 0.5-0.7 (0.6), put math instructions and \\boxed{} in the user prompt, force '<think>\\n'. The paper says few-shot hurts."),
 ("Why avoid greedy decoding for R1-distill?", "README warns of endless repetitions at low temperature; so we sample at T=0.6. This makes G20 non-deterministic and is why we test consistency across seeds."),
 ("Does the R1 repo contain code?", "No - only README.md, DeepSeek_R1.pdf, figures and LICENSE. Architecture is in transformers' Qwen2."),
 ("Where is Gemma-1 code in the Gemma repo?", "In 2024 history (commit 59ffafe): gemma/transformer.py, modules.py, layers.py, positional_embeddings.py, sampler.py. Main now documents newer models."),
 ("How does Gemma's reference sampler decode?", "Greedy: jnp.argmax over logits in Sampler._sample_step."),
 ("Why does the 7B R1-distill not fit a T4 in fp16?", "Weights are 15.2 GB on disk, over the T4's ~15 GB before activations. We use 4-bit NF4 and record it as a confounder."),
 ("What is NF4 / bitsandbytes?", "A 4-bit normal-float quantisation for weights with higher-precision compute; cuts memory ~3-4x with some accuracy loss."),
 ("Why is the comparison not perfectly fair?", "Different size (2B vs 7B), precision (bf16/fp16 vs 4-bit), decoding (greedy vs sampling), token budgets, specialisation (general vs reasoning) and possibly GPU."),
 ("Can you say which model is better?", "Only per task/metric within our 30-sample set and with caveats; no universal-winner claim."),
 ("How was the dataset built?", "30 independently authored prompts, 10 categories x 3; items 1-2 per category are dev (20), item 3 is held-out test (10); test prompts never used for tuning."),
 ("Why a dev/test split if nothing is trained?", "Prompt format, checker rules and decoding settings are tuned on dev only so test remains an unbiased check of the whole pipeline."),
 ("Is 10 test samples statistically meaningful?", "No: Wilson 95% intervals are wide (e.g. 5/10 spans roughly 24%-76%). We report intervals and avoid strong claims."),
 ("Define accuracy, EM and token F1.", "Accuracy = rule-checker correct / n. EM = normalised string equality with the reference. F1 = token overlap harmonic mean; useful for short answers."),
 ("What is ROUGE and its limit?", "N-gram / LCS overlap between summary and reference; ignores meaning and factuality. We use our own implementation without stemming."),
 ("How is reasoning correctness defined?", "For logical/multi-step items, whether the final answer extracted after </think> (or from the response) is right, tracked separately from surface string match."),
 ("How do you grade code?", "Extract the code block, run unit tests in a subprocess with timeout; pass/fail."),
 ("How do you evaluate structured output?", "Parse as JSON/CSV/markdown table/key-value and check schema constraints; reports validity separately from correctness."),
 ("What robustness variations did you run?", "Five: prompt wording, input complexity, ambiguous instructions, math complexity, structured formats - 26 prompts, saved with input, expected, actual, evaluation, time, observation."),
 ("What failure classes can appear?", "Maths error, logical error, factual inaccuracy, instruction violation, invalid structure, coding error, ambiguity mishandling, truncation/endless thinking. Only observed failures are reported; theoretical ones are labelled."),
 ("What resource experiments were designed?", "Precision (bf16/fp16/8-bit/4-bit), input length (needle prompts) and generation length; each records time, allocated/reserved/peak memory."),
 ("Why torch.cuda.synchronize in timing?", "CUDA kernels are asynchronous; without synchronising, wall-clock timing would miss GPU work."),
 ("Allocated vs reserved vs peak memory?", "Allocated = live tensors; reserved = memory held by the caching allocator; peak = max allocated since reset."),
 ("How do you split reasoning from answer for R1?", "Split on '</think>'; if the tag never closes the sample is flagged 'unfinished thinking' and counted as truncation."),
 ("Why is R1-distill slower per question?", "It emits long chain-of-thought tokens; time scales with generated tokens, which our logs record (tokens/sec and mean new tokens)."),
 ("What would you do with more time/compute?", "Larger dataset, multiple seeds per prompt, bf16 7B on an A100 for a precision-matched comparison, standard benchmarks with the papers' protocols."),
 ("What did you NOT do?", "No pretraining, no RL, no fine-tuning. This is an inference and evaluation study only."),
 ("What is the honest status of the results?", "Delivered notebooks are executable end to end in Colab; this package was authored without a GPU, so numbers are only present if the user ran the notebooks and rebuilt the reports."),
]
def viva_blocks():
    b = [("p", "Answers are short viva-ready summaries grounded in the papers and repositories studied; sources: [GP] Gemma paper, [DP] DeepSeek-R1 paper, [DR] repo README. Questions about our measured numbers must be answered from your own Colab run.")]
    for n, (q, a) in enumerate(VIVA, 1):
        b += [("h3", "Q%d. %s" % (n, q)), ("p", a)]
    return b
